WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.800
The benefits of regular exercise are well documented but there’s a new bonus to add to the ever-growing list.
经常锻炼的好处早已得到充分证实，而现在，这份不断加长的清单上又可以添上一项新的好处。

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:21.490
New research found that middle-aged women who were physically fit could be nearly 90 percent less likely to develop dementia in later life, and if they did, it came on a decade later than in less sporty women.
新研究发现，中年时身体素质好的女性日后患痴呆的可能性或许会低近90%；即使患病，发病时间也比运动较少的女性晚十年。

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:38.060
Lead researcher Dr. Helena Horder, of the University of Gothenburg in Sweden, said: “These findings are exciting because it’s possible that improving people’s cardiovascular fitness in middle age could delay dementia or even prevent them from developing it.”
首席研究员、瑞典哥德堡大学的海伦娜·霍德博士说：“这些发现令人振奋，因为在中年时提高人们的心血管健康水平，有可能延缓痴呆的发生，甚至预防他们患上痴呆。”

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:49.770
For the study, 191 women with an average age of 50 took a bicycle exercise test until they were exhausted to measure their peak cardiovascular capacity.
在这项研究中，191名平均年龄为50岁的女性进行了自行车运动测试，一直骑到筋疲力尽，以测量她们的心血管能力峰值。

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.130
The average peak workload was measured at 103 watts.
测得的平均峰值负荷为103瓦。

00:00:54.930 --> 00:01:00.950
A total of 40 women met the criteria for a high fitness level, or 120 watts or higher.
共有40名女性达到高体能水平的标准，即峰值负荷达到120瓦或以上。

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:18.812
A total of 92 women were in the medium fitness category; and 59 women were in the low fitness category, defined as a peak workload of 80 watts or less, or having their exercise tests stopped because of high blood pressure, chest pain or other cardiovascular problems.
共有92名女性属于中等体能类别；59名女性属于低体能类别，其定义为峰值负荷在80瓦及以下，或因高血压、胸痛或其他心血管问题而中止运动测试。

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:24.472
These women were then tested for dementia six times over the following four decades.
在随后的四十年里，这些女性接受了六次痴呆检测。

00:01:25.272 --> 00:01:28.982
During that time, 44 of the women developed dementia.
在此期间，其中44名女性患上了痴呆。

00:01:29.782 --> 00:01:40.002
Five percent of the highly fit women developed dementia, compared to 25 percent of the women with medium fitness and 32 percent of the women with low fitness.
高体能女性中有5%患上了痴呆，相比之下，中等体能女性中这一比例为25%，低体能女性中为32%。

00:01:40.802 --> 00:01:48.714
“However, this study does not show cause and effect between cardiovascular fitness and dementia; it only shows an association.
“不过，这项研究并未显示心血管健康与痴呆之间存在因果关系；它只显示了二者之间的关联。

00:01:49.514 --> 00:02:00.184
More research is needed to see if improved fitness could have a positive effect on the risk of dementia and also to look at when during a lifetime a high fitness level is most important.”
还需要进一步研究，看看提高体能是否会对痴呆风险产生积极影响，同时也要研究人一生中什么时候保持高体能水平最为重要。”

00:02:00.984 --> 00:02:09.354
She also admitted that a relatively small number of women were studied, all of whom were from Sweden, so the results might not be applicable to other groups.
她也承认，参与研究的女性人数相对较少，而且全都来自瑞典，因此研究结果可能并不适用于其他群体。
